### Get all users
GET http://localhost:3000/api/users

###

### Get user by ID (replace with actual ObjectId from create response)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/users/507f1f77bcf86cd799439011

###

### Create new user (coach)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "coach_john",
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "password_hash": "$2b$10$abcdefghijklmnopqrstuv",
  "role": "coach"
}

###

### Update user (replace with actual ObjectId from create response)
PUT http://localhost:3000/api/users/507f1f77bcf86cd799439011
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "coach_john_updated",
  "email": "john.doe.updated@example.com",
  "role": "manager"
}

###

### Delete user (replace with actual ObjectId from create response)
DELETE http://localhost:3000/api/users/507f1f77bcf86cd799439012

### Delete ALL users (WARNING: This will delete all users in the database!)
DELETE http://localhost:3000/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

###

### ===== ERROR SCENARIO TESTS =====

### 2. POST request which fails validation - Invalid email
POST http://localhost:3000/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "test_user",
  "email": "invalid-email",
  "password_hash": "$2b$10$abcdefghijklmnopqrstuv",
  "role": "coach"
}

###

### POST request which fails validation - Short username
POST http://localhost:3000/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "ab",
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password_hash": "$2b$10$abcdefghijklmnopqrstuv",
  "role": "coach"
}

###

### POST request which fails validation - Invalid role
POST http://localhost:3000/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "test_user",
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password_hash": "$2b$10$abcdefghijklmnopqrstuv",
  "role": "invalid_role"
}

